{
  "$comment": "NEW. The rule for choosing a wrong answer. A distractor drawn at random teaches nothing; a distractor that differs from the target on exactly one dimension makes the error diagnostic — the app then knows WHICH discrimination failed and can drill it. `visual` drives tap-identify and missing-letter; `auditory` drives listen-choose and syllable-build. Every candidate is filtered against the lesson's decodability set before it can be used, so a distractor is never a letter she has not met.",
  "rules": [
    "A distractor MUST appear in decodability.json for the item's lesson.",
    "Prefer a confusion-matrix neighbour; fall back to a random decodable item only when the matrix is exhausted.",
    "Never use more than one grapheme-length distractor per item in Unit 1 or 2.",
    "The correct answer's position is drawn from the seeded RNG, never fixed.",
    "Two consecutive items in the same activity may not share a distractor set."
  ],
